Notebook[{Cell["Transversely polarized proton-proton classes (A_TT), step 1: \
diagrams and amplitudes of one class", "Title"], 
  Cell["Single-inclusive parton production in collisions of two transversely \
polarized protons, a(pa) + b(pb) -> c(p) + X, at NLO in QCD for the five \
channel classes of classes.wl (5, 6, 7, 11, 12 in the numbering of \
Processes/Hadronic): both incoming partons are quarks or antiquarks carrying \
a transverse spin, the observed parton is unpolarized.  The variable class \
below selects the class; every step of this process starts with it, and the \
results are stored under Results/<route>/class-<n>/.\n\nThe diagrams are \
those of Processes/Hadronic (the same FeynArts generation, the same amplitude \
records): for the chosen class this step generates the Born process a b -> c \
d (when it exists), its one-loop corrections, and every real-emission process \
a b -> c d e of the class with its weight (identical unobserved partons, \
flavour multiplicities).  The transverse spin enters only in step 2, through \
the spin densities of the two incoming partons.\n\nMomenta: pa, pb incoming; \
p the observed parton; k1, k2 the unobserved partons (k1 + k2 = pa + pb - p); \
loop the loop momentum.  Flavours: q = quark of flavour i (up quark of \
FeynArts' SMQCD model), qp = quark of flavour k (charm), g = gluon; closed \
quark loops run over all three generations of the model and are counted with \
the symbol Nf in step 2.", "Text"], Cell["Load the package and the class", 
   "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \
\"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["LoadFeynCalc[]", "Input"], Cell["class = \
\"5\";\nGet[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"classes.wl\"}]];\nRequire[KeyExistsQ[HadronicTTClasses, \
ToExpression[class]], \"Not a class of the transversely polarized process (5, \
6, 7, 11, 12)\", class];\nspec = \
HadronicTTClasses[ToExpression[class]];\nPrint[\"Class \", class, \": \", \
spec[\"Name\"]];\nspec", "Input"], Cell["Generate the diagrams", "Section"], 
  Cell["FeynArts fields: F[3,{1}] the up quark (flavour i), F[3,{2}] the \
charm quark (flavour k), V[5] the gluon, U[5] the gluon ghost (only in \
loops).  Everything else of the SMQCD model (photon, weak bosons, Higgs, \
leptons, down-type quarks, the third generation as an external particle) is \
excluded.  The observed parton is the first outgoing particle of each \
process; the tadpole topologies and the self-energy corrections on external \
legs are excluded from the one-loop generation (they are scaleless and vanish \
for massless partons).", "Text"], Cell["field = <|\"q\" -> F[3, {1}], \"qb\" \
-> -F[3, {1}], \"qp\" -> F[3, {2}], \"qpb\" -> -F[3, {2}], \"g\" -> \
V[5]|>;\nexcluded = {S[_], V[1 | 2 | 3], F[1 | 2 | 4]};\ngenerate[loops_, \
in_, out_] := InsertFields[CreateTopologies[loops, Length[in] -> \
Length[out],\n    ExcludeTopologies -> If[loops == 0, {}, {Tadpoles, \
WFCorrections}]],\n  (field /@ in) -> (field /@ out), InsertionLevel -> \
{Classes}, Model -> \"SMQCD\",\n  ExcludeParticles -> Join[excluded, If[loops \
== 0, {U[_]}, {}]]];\nbornDiagrams = If[spec[\"Born\"] === None, None, \
generate[0, spec[\"Born\"][[1 ;; 2]], spec[\"Born\"][[3 ;; \
4]]]];\nvirtualDiagrams = If[spec[\"Virtual\"], generate[1, spec[\"Born\"][[1 \
;; 2]], spec[\"Born\"][[3 ;; 4]]], None];\nrealDiagrams = Association @ \
Table[StringRiffle[proc[[1]], \" \"] -> generate[0, proc[[1]][[1 ;; 2]], \
proc[[1]][[3 ;; 5]]], {proc, spec[\"Real\"]}];\n<|\"Born\" -> If[bornDiagrams \
=== None, 0, Length[bornDiagrams]], \"Virtual\" -> If[virtualDiagrams === \
None, 0, Length[virtualDiagrams]],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[Length, \
realDiagrams]|>", "Input"], Cell["If[bornDiagrams =!= None, \
Paint[bornDiagrams, ColumnsXRows -> {Min[Length[bornDiagrams], 4], 1}, \
Numbering -> Simple, SheetHeader -> None, ImageSize -> {170 \
Min[Length[bornDiagrams], 4], 170}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Amplitudes", "Section"], Cell["FCFAConvert rewrites the FeynArts \
amplitudes in FeynCalc notation without contracting anything; quark masses \
are set to zero, the gauge parameter to one (Feynman gauge).  The one-loop \
amplitudes keep the loop momentum loop.  The third-generation quark running \
in closed loops appears with the symbolic FeynArts generation sum, which step \
2 replaces by the number of flavours Nf.", "Text"], 
  Cell["convert[diagrams_, in_, out_, loops_: {}] := \
FCFAConvert[CreateFeynAmp[diagrams, Truncated -> False, PreFactor -> 1],\n  \
IncomingMomenta -> in, OutgoingMomenta -> out, LoopMomenta -> loops, \
UndoChiralSplittings -> True, ChangeDimension -> D,\n  List -> True, SMP -> \
False, Contract -> False, DropSumOver -> False,\n  FinalSubstitutions -> \
{FCGV[\"MU\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MC\"] -> 0, FCGV[\"MT\"] -> 0, SMP[\"g_s\"] -> \
gs}] /. GaugeXi[_] -> 1 /. MQU[_] -> 0;   (* MQU: mass of the loop quark of \
generic generation *)\namplitudes = <|\n  \"Born\" -> If[bornDiagrams === \
None, {}, convert[bornDiagrams, {pa, pb}, {p, k1}]],\n  \"Virtual\" -> \
If[virtualDiagrams === None, {}, convert[virtualDiagrams, {pa, pb}, {p, k1}, \
{loop}]],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[convert[#, {pa, pb}, {p, k1, k2}] &, \
realDiagrams]|>;\nLength /@ Append[Map[Length, amplitudes[\"Real\"]], \
\"Virtual\" -> amplitudes[\"Virtual\"]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Closed quark loops: FeynArts sums the generation index of a closed \
fermion loop (SumOver[Index[Generation, n], 3]); the loop amplitudes are the \
same for every massless flavour, so each such amplitude counts Nf times.  \
Amplitudes with an external-generation sum do not occur because every \
external flavour is fixed.", "Text"], Cell["flavourSum = \
SumOver[Index[Generation, _], 3] -> Nf;\nRequire[FreeQ[amplitudes, \
SumOver[Index[Generation, _], _, External]], \"An external generation sum \
appeared\"];\namplitudes = amplitudes /. flavourSum /. SumOver[__] -> 1;      \
(* the colour sums are implicit in the colour algebra of step 2 \
*)\nCount[amplitudes[\"Virtual\"], Nf, Infinity]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Records", "Section"], Cell["records = <|\"Born\" -> AmplitudeRecords \
/@ amplitudes[\"Born\"], \"Virtual\" -> AmplitudeRecords /@ \
amplitudes[\"Virtual\"],\n  \"Real\" -> Map[AmplitudeRecords /@ # &, \
amplitudes[\"Real\"]]|>;\nRequire[FreeQ[records, $Failed], \"A record could \
not be formed\"];\nweights = Association @ Table[StringRiffle[proc[[1]], \" \
\"] -> proc[[2]], {proc, spec[\"Real\"]}];\nSaveAmplitudes[<|\"FeynCalc\" -> \
amplitudes, \"Records\" -> records, \"Class\" -> class, \"Spec\" -> spec, \
\"Weights\" -> weights|>, \"class-\" <> \
class];\nShowRecords[Flatten[records[\"Born\"]]]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
